<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tokhtamysh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1406</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tokhtamysh (died 1406) was a Mongol khan descended from Jochi who, with the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>, became khan of the White Horde and by 1380 reunited it with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>. He sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> in 1382, restoring Mongol overlordship over the Russian principalities, but then turned against Timur, who defeated him in 1391 and on the Terek in 1395. He was killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> in 1406.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh.jpg" alt="Tokhtamysh" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1436 painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_between_Timur_and_Toqtamish_Khan_in_1391._Zafarnama_of_1436_(Toqtamish_detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
